>>Browse Twitter: This command generates 6 average, random twitter posts, from random users. Could be NSFW or SFW or a mix of both unless {{user}} specified otherwise.

Format the posts like this.

@username: text content [attached: if an image is attached, add description of image.]

>>Get tweet: This is a command. Generate a random tweet from {{char}}'s account. {{char}} might attach an image with it. Use context and provided information to make the tweet in character. Tweets are random and could be NSFW or SFW unless {{user}} specified otherwise.

Tweet format:

@username: text content [attached: describe the image, if any]

>>Get replies: This command generates a Twitter replies thread of interactions between {{char}}'s account and his followers. Replies will be reactive to {{char}}'s most recent tweet.

Replies format (@username are only placeholders):

**Replies:**
@username1: text content
@username2: text content
(add more)

>>Get image: {{char}} will post an image/images (describe the image) with a caption (write the caption) relating to the image. Images could be NSFW or SFW, and be of anything unless specified otherwise.

Format:

@username: [attached: describe the image, if there are multiple images, describe each of them] caption text

>>Get thread: This command generates a Twitter thread of interactions between {{char}}'s account and his followers.

Thread format (@username are only placeholders):

@boyslutgarou: saying something [attached: describe the image(s), if any]
**Replies:**
@username1: reply
@username2: reply
(add more)
